UWW's own scouting notes for Carroll (WI) Pioneers [SOURCE: SCOUTING REPORT]:
  KEYS TO VICTORY: 1. TRANSITION DEFENSE!!! | 2. SQUEEZE & LIMIT #4 (Guard 1 on 1 + Gap Help) | 3. ATTACK THE PAINT OFFENSIVELY!!
  TEAM STRENGTHS: 1. Fast paced offense (quick ball movement & cutting) | 2. Main scorer #4 capable of carrying offense (23 ppg) | 3. Push hard in transition

--- Comparing PBP evidence to the stated Keys to Victory [SOURCE: SCOUTING REPORT] ---

KEY 1 [SCOUTING REPORT] -- COMMUNICATE SCREENS & ACTIONS:
  Not directly measurable from play-by-play event types (no screen-action tagging) -- this is a
  communication/technique key tied to their offensive scheme (per the scout's own Offensive Scheme notes),
  not something the event log alone can confirm or refute.

KEY 2 [SCOUTING REPORT] -- DOMINATE THE PAINT:
  Their own rebounding split across their 26 games: [{'rebound_type': 'defensive', 'count': 658}, {'rebound_type': 'offensive', 'count': 324}]
  Their layup-area attempts (Layup + Driving Layup): 744 of 1453 total FGA
  Blocks recorded against them by opponents: 102
  Compare against their own Defensive Scheme notes and layup-area conversion rate to judge whether this key
  is supported by the evidence.

KEY 3 [SCOUTING REPORT] -- GUARD 1 ON 1:
  Measured 3PT jump-shot rate: 582 attempts at 33.5%.
  Scoring balance (top 5 scorers): [{'player': 'Michael McNabb', 'total_points_across_26_games': 558.0}, {'player': 'Lamar Smith', 'total_points_across_26_games': 436.0}, {'player': 'Peyton McKenna', 'total_points_across_26_games': 266.0}, {'player': 'Jacob Naber', 'total_points_across_26_games': 247.0}, {'player': 'Dennis Estepp', 'total_points_across_26_games': 166.0}]
  Compare against the scout's own TEAM STRENGTHS note on shooting/scoring balance to judge whether
  over-helping creates open catch-and-shoot looks that straight man coverage would limit.


--- New Keys to Victory, derived from PBP data/tendencies [SOURCE: PBP-DERIVED] ---

DATA-KEY 1 [PBP-DERIVED] -- TAKE AWAY THEIR MOST EFFICIENT HIGH-VOLUME ACTIONS:
  Offensive Rebound: 69.0% on 29 attempts; Cut: 68.5% on 92 attempts
  Each is 5+ points above their 47.1% overall clip on 15+ attempts. Offensive Rebound: hit a body on every shot before going to the ball. Cut: jump to the ball on every pass and see man and ball -- no back-cuts behind ball-watchers.

DATA-KEY 2 [PBP-DERIVED] -- FUNNEL THEM INTO THEIR WORST HIGH-VOLUME LOOKS:
  Off Screen: 32.3% on 31 attempts; P&R Ball Handler: 36.4% on 162 attempts
  Each is 5+ points below their 47.1% overall clip -- don't help off these actions; make them keep taking them.

DATA-KEY 3 [PBP-DERIVED] -- PRESSURE THE ACTIONS THEY TURN IT OVER ON:
  P&R Ball Handler: 48 TO in 210 uses (22.9% vs 13.8% across all actions); ISO: 12 TO in 59 uses (20.3% vs 13.8% across all actions)
  Loosest actions per use, not the most common ones -- load ball pressure and gap help onto these specifically rather than pressing everything.


